# Upper Town (no puzzles)
dialogue nell
  node root nell "You're the clerk from the customs house. Buying, or loitering? I only charge for one of them."
    > "What are you selling?" -> selling
    > "Tell me about the village." -> village
    > "Anything odd happening lately?" -> odd
    > "Just looking. Goodnight." -> bye
  node selling nell "Rope, lamp oil, dried fish, and gossip. The fish is fresher than the gossip, and neither is fresh."
    > "I'll take the gossip." -> odd
    > "Another time." -> bye
  node village nell "Forty houses and a well. Half of them empty since the ships stopped coming back. The other half are related to each other, which is the real reason it's quiet."
    > "Empty why?" -> odd
    > "It looks peaceful." -> peaceful
  node peaceful nell "It is. That's what worries me. A harbour town should sound like a harbour."
    > "Goodnight, Nell." -> bye
  node odd nell "Six ships in three years. Five found drifting, sails set, nobody aboard; the sixth not found at all. The insurers call it weather. Weather doesn't tie off a wheel."
    > "You've seen one of them." -> wheel
    > "You think someone took them." -> taken
  node wheel nell "I sold rope to the men who towed them in. Wheel lashed amidships, every one, boats still hanging. Whatever happened, they weren't fighting it."
    > "That isn't weather." -> taken
  node taken nell "No. It isn't. But I sell rope, clerk, not answers. Ask the old woman on the steps — she lost people, and she isn't afraid to say so."
    > "I will. Goodnight." -> bye
  node bye nell "Go on. Hear anything out there, I'm buying. News, I mean. Not rope."
  # Act IV: the news, arriving at a run.
  node news nell "Clerk! They're saying the Marrow came in with a hundred and thirty dead men aboard, and the dead men are buying drinks. Tell me it's true. I've sold it twice already."
    > "It's true. All of it." -> true
    > "You were right, Nell. Weather doesn't tie off a wheel." if seen:nell.wheel -> wheel4
  node true nell "Then I'll put my prices up. …Go on. Old Onn's been on that step for three years, waiting for somebody in particular, and I think it's you."
  node wheel4 nell "I said that. I said it three years ago, to anybody who'd buy a herring. Write down that I said it, clerk. I want it in a ledger somewhere."
